  "summary": "Several studies directly apply federated learning techniques, specifically described as 'decentralised training without pooled records', to the problem of predicting customer attrition [V0201, V0203, V0202, V0204]. These methods are evaluated across various datasets including ChurnBench, Atlas-ICU, MetroFlow, and AgriSat-4, reporting performance metrics such as accuracy, AUROC, MAE, and F1 scores ranging from 0.64 to 0.92. Additionally, self-attention encoder models have been deployed for this task on the ChurnBench dataset [V0197].",
